<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marad was an ancient Sumerian city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nippur">Nippur</a>, identified with the mound of Tell Wanna wa Sadum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. Its patron god was Lugal-Marada. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akkadian-empire">Akkadian Empire</a> a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naram-sin">Naram-Sin</a> governed it, and in the early second millennium BCE it lay in the sphere of the kingdoms of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazallu">Kazallu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>.</p></div>
